Name: jmap_require_accountid
Type: SWITCH
Default-Value: 0
Last-Modified: UNRELEASED
Deprecated-Since: UNRELEASED

This option once allowed a JMAP method call to omit the "accountId"
argument, which was then taken to mean the authenticated user's own
account.  It is now ignored: as RFC 8620 requires, every method other than
Core/echo rejects a missing, null or non-string "accountId" with an
"invalidArguments" error.
